notes               = "Printed with a title above the verse, so english_title renders the poet's own Persian title. The title line is lifted out of the body. The date line is also a provenance line — بهمن ۱۳۶۹ در پاسخ به مجلهٔ گردون, 'Bahman 1369, in reply to Gardoon magazine' — so this was written to order for a magazine; that half is kept in ===footnotes=== rather than the body. دههٔ شصت is the Solar Hijri ۱۳۶۰s (1981-1991), the war decade, NOT the Gregorian sixties; a translator must not let it read as 1960s. The closing lines in guillemets are the 'proverb' the poet says he has never heard anywhere — i.e. he made it. The leaves-and-roots lines return almost verbatim fourteen years later on page 193 (leaves-roots). Bahman is a winter month, so +622 → 1991. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
